Z||000001||rmorgandotcom||10-12-2001||12:08 AM||||The Fino is advertised as a component kit, very similar to my finale.  However, I'm pretty sure that the rear end is a bit wider than the fiero.(and uses different rockers)<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/rmorgansig.jpg">    <BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE> <BR><LI><I><FONT COLOR="blue">project - finale body on a 86 4 cylinder 5 speed</FONT></I><BR><LI><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/rmorgandotcom/</A><BR></UL><p>[This message has been edited by rmorgandotcom (edited 10-12-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||10-12-2001||12:28 AM||||Not really. Look at rmogandotcom's sig pic just above this post..see how its "smooth" from the top of the door to the rear end? Well, a Fino kit has taller door panels than stock Fieros. So if you put a Fino rear end on an otherwise stock Fiero, its be "outta line" from the doors back..it wont look right.||||reg||1
